umbnail":""},{"id":"1775588039623","neuronKeys":["[#1cb4f]"],"edgeStrings":["[#69678]_#_[#1cb4f]","[#1cb4f]_#_[#203d5]","[#1cb4f]_#_[#cd80b]"],"description":"When SpikerBot gets too close to an obstacle, it will automatically back up to avoid a crash.","thumbnail":""},{"id":"1775588085973","neuronKeys":["[#ed194]"],"edgeStrings":[],"description":"We can also trigger a sequence to avoid pedestrians when we press ‘X’ on our gamepad.you can set this also to respond to any button or keyboard key.","thumbnail":""},{"id":"1775588141265","neuronKeys":["[#ed194]","[#ceb00]","[#e2cd6]"],"edgeStrings":["[#ed194]_#_[#e2cd6]","[#ed194]_#_[#ceb00]","[#ceb00]_#_[#e2cd6]"],"description":"When you first press the ‘x’ button, these three neurons will trigger together, with the bottom neuron triggering only once via Feed Forward Inhibition.","thumbnail":""},{"id":"1775588200208","neuronKeys":["[#e2cd6]","[#ed194]"],"edgeStrings":["[#e2cd6]_#_[#1fb03]","[#e2cd6]_#_[#bcb0e]","[#ed194]_#_[#e2cd6]"],"description":"We will blink warning lights once, and SpikerBot will say ‘Uh-oh’ when we first activate pedestrian avoidance.","thumbnail":""},{"id":"1775588344709","neuronKeys":["[#cb6e2]","[#621e4]"],"edgeStrings":["[#5bb2b]_#_[#cb6e2]","[#5bb2b]_#_[#621e4]","[#621e4]_#_[#cd80b]","[#cb6e2]_#_[#203d5]"],"description":"These two neurons will make SpikerBot scared of other people. Each neuron responds when a person is in the right or left field of view. SpikerBot will back up while facing them to avoid the person while keeping them in view.","thumbnail":""},{"id":"1775588404266","neuronKeys":["[#1bb53]"],"edgeStrings":["[#1bb53]_#_[#621e4]","[#1bb53]_#_[#cb6e2]","[#1bb53]_#_[#1cb4f]"],"description":"This highly active Inhiitory neuron will fire without any input. It keeps obstacle avoidance, and crash avoidance networks off while you are driving around freely.","thumbnail":""},{"id":"1775588456952","neuronKeys":["[#ed194]","[#ceb00]","[#1bb53]"],"edgeStrings":["[#ed194]_#_[#ceb00]","[#ceb00]_#_[#1bb53]"],"description":"When you turn on obstacle and pedestrian avoidance, we disable the blocking inhibitory cell, allowing the other behaviors to respond to distance input and camera targets realtime.","thumbnail":""},{"id":"1775588566134","neuronKeys":["[#4cde5]","[#cc7c8]","[#ed8a2]"],"edgeStrings":["[#4cde5]_#_[#cc7c8]","[#4cde5]_#_[#ed8a2]","[#cc7c8]_#_[#ed8a2]","[#ed8a2]_#_[#bcb0e]","[#ed8a2]_#_[#1fb03]"],"description":"When we are done avoiding obstacles and people, we want to alert everyone that the road in clear. Here we have another Feed Forward Inhibition network where the output triggers only once. The top input neuron is not quiet but is made highly active, so this wants to trigger all the time, when we arent pressing buttons.","thumbnail":""},{"id":"1775588640155","neuronKeys":["[#ed194]","[#ceb00]","[#4cde5]"],"edgeStrings":["[#ed194]_#_[#ceb00]","[#ceb00]_#_[#4cde5]"],"description":"Hen we release the ‘x’ button, it allows the highly active excitatory neuron at the end of the chain to begin firing, and trigger the Feed Forward Inhibition circuit downstream one time.","thumbnail":""},{"id":"1775588679731","neuronKeys":["[#65679]"],"edgeStrings":["[#65679]_#_[#bcb0e]","[#65679]_#_[#1fb03]"],"description":"You can also beep SpikeBot’s horn at any time by pressing the left trigger button ‘L2’","thumbnail":""},{"id":"1775588736356","neuronKeys":["[#ed194]","[#ceb00]","[#e2cd6]"],"edgeStrings":["[#ed194]_#_[#e2cd6]","[#ed194]_#_[#ceb00]","[#ceb00]_#_[#e2cd6]"],"description":"What other behaviors can you add to the car to make it more interesting? Can you activate other self driving functions with a button press?","thumbnail":""}],"info":{"title":"This Car is Scared of People","description":"Drive SpikerBot like a remote control car and avoid pedestrians on command.","author":"User","version":"1.0.1","timestamp":"2026-04-08T16:04:13.812097"}}